        "original_id": "a922683d-e964-5945-86f4-e9307533780c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: University of New Haven, Carnegie Mellon University, Lyme Academy College of Fine Arts\n- Places: West Haven, New Haven, Connecticut, Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, Old Lyme, Long Island Sound\n- Topics: private universities, research universities, art colleges, constituent colleges\n\nFacts:\n- The University of New Haven is a private, nonsectarian, coeducational university located in West Haven, Connecticut, near New Haven and Long Island Sound.\n- Carnegie Mellon University is a private research university located in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania.\n- Since 2014, Lyme Academy College of Fine Arts in Old Lyme, Connecticut, has been a constituent college of the University of New Haven.",
